      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cron): bound cron quarantine sidecar file reads",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`loadCronQuarantineFile` in `src/cron/store.ts` reads the cron quarantine sidecar with an unbounded `fs.promises.readFile` call. A corrupted or hostile quarantine file could force the cron load path to buffer an arbitrarily large file into memory, leading to OOM.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nQuarantine sidecars are small JSON files. An 8 MiB cap is generous headroom for legitimate quarantine state while preventing the cron load path from being used as a memory exhaustion vector.\n\n## User Impact\n\nLoading a cron quarantine file that exceeds the safe cap now fails fast with a clear size-limit error instead of risking process OOM.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added a regression test that writes a quarantine file exceeding the 8 MiB cap and asserts `loadCronQuarantineFile` rejects with `File exceeds 8388608 bytes`.\n- Local focused run: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/cron/store.test.ts --run` passes (47/47 tests).\n\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nI ran a standalone non-test script that imports the real `loadCronQuarantineFile` from `src/cron/store.ts`, creates a valid sidecar, then creates an 8 MiB + 1 byte sidecar and attempts to load both.\n\nCommand:\n\n```text\n$ node --import tsx /tmp/proof-101477.mjs\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```text\n=== Normal quarantine sidecar ===\npath: /tmp/proof-cron-quarantine-normal-1783420207397.json\nloaded: {\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"jobs\": [\n    {\n      \"quarantinedAtMs\": 1783420207397,\n      \"sourceIndex\": 0,\n      \"reason\": \"invalid schedule\",\n      \"job\": {\n        \"id\": \"test-job\",\n        \"schedule\": \"not-a-cron\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n=== Oversized quarantine sidecar ===\npath: /tmp/proof-cron-quarantine-oversized-1783420207397.json\nsize: 8388609 bytes (> 8388608 byte cap)\nrejected: File exceeds 8388608 bytes: /tmp/proof-cron-quarantine-oversized-1783420207397.json\n```\n\nThe normal sidecar loads and parses successfully. The oversized sidecar is rejected before any JSON parsing or downstream cron processing occurs, with the bounded reader returning `File exceeds 8388608 bytes`.\n\n- Also added a regression test that asserts `saveCronQuarantineFile` rejects before writing a sidecar whose JSON payload would exceed the same 8 MiB cap, preventing OpenClaw from creating a sidecar it cannot later load.\n\n",
        "branch": "fix/bound-cron-quarantine-read",
